# Reviewed sibling revisions. This file is the single executable source of
# truth for which kafkars stack the benchmark lab measures; every other
# consumer (scripts/check-dependency-provenance, .github/actions/checkout-
# siblings, evidence bundles) reads these three assignments and nothing else.
#
# THE PIN RULE — the three lines are not independent knobs:
#
#   KAFKARS_REVISION         the reviewed commit of kafkars/kafkars main that
#                            this repository benchmarks. This is the only line
#                            a human chooses.
#
#   KAFKA_DRIVER_REVISION    MUST equal the values committed in THAT Kafkars
#   KAFKA_PROTOCOL_REVISION  revision's own dependencies/sibling-revisions.env.
#                            They are copied, never picked.
#
# So bumping the Kafkars pin is a two-step edit, in this order:
#
#   git -C ../kafkars show <new-kafkars-revision>:dependencies/sibling-revisions.env
#
# then paste both values below verbatim. scripts/check-dependency-provenance
# re-derives that cross-check on every run and fails CI when the three lines
# disagree, because a benchmark bundle that names a Kafkars commit while linking
# a different driver is evidence about a stack nobody reviewed.
#
# A fourth repository is read but never pinned here: scripts/check-dependency-
# provenance also cross-checks the `kafka_wire_revision` that kafka-driver's own
# guardrails.toml declares against KAFKA_PROTOCOL_REVISION below, because a
# driver that names a different wire revision than this lab pins is a stack
# nobody reviewed. The public kafka-wire repository is checked out locally as
# `kafka-protocol`, matching the path dependency in kafkars/kafkars.
#
# Format is load-bearing: exactly three assignments, in this order, each a
# lowercase 40-hex commit id. Comments and blank lines are ignored.
KAFKARS_REVISION=ccbbae91ef6fda6a2d3adaa83c60c294b3c54cb2
KAFKA_DRIVER_REVISION=626494bcf0d9a48895e540e1031f7be1750f3d2b
KAFKA_PROTOCOL_REVISION=e2b95c1ce06896603ff9ac96dc0e0206bbf58085
